the northern realms are a dangerous  place but with New Game+ coming to the  witcher 3 there couldn't be a better  time to hone those witcher skills and  take a stab at the game's hardest  difficulty death march if you do plan on  undertaking this challenge here are some  tips and tricks every witcher should  live by  now this may seem like a basic one but  it's something that even the more  seasoned witchers shouldn't overlook  especially during the first ten or so  hours of the game just because you could  scrape through a fight on the normal  difficulty with low health it doesn't  mean you can on death march sometimes  you have to embrace that flight  mentality and run for the hills if your  health is low or if you are thin on  resources sometimes the best idea is  usually to hop on your trusty steed  Roach and ride on out of there in most  cases whoever or whatever you're hunting  will be waiting for you when you are  better equipped Geralt has two evasive  moves he can roll or he can dodge  rolling creates more distance between  Geralt and his foe but it also drains  stamina now dodging on the other hand  let's go outside step away from attacks  without sucking up any of his precious  stamina unless you intend to run it is  in your best interest to learn how to  dodge effectively not only does dodging  spare your stamina but it also keeps  Geralt within arm's reach of his foes  making it much easier to get in a few  strikes before the enemy can reposition  themselves right from the get-go you  should start sinking your ability points  Indic when it is hands-down the most  useful spell on harder difficulties  because it essentially lets you take an  extra hit or two depending on how you've  leveled it up no matter what kind of  build you are going for I'd recommend  leveling up the active shield ability  this will allow you to recover health  when you are hit before you approach a  group of enemies cask when as long as  you see a gold spark circling girl it  means his shield is ready to deflect any  kind of blow thrown at him after you've  been hit back off and wait for your  stamina to recharge once it's up cast  the spell again and take up an offensive  position death march is designed to  force you to prepare for fights if you  are walking into a big fight or if  you're at the tail end of a monster  contract don't neglect your friendly  merchants scattered throughout the land  make sure you are stocked up on food  water and of course those tasty chicken  sandwiches research which you are  hunting make sure your potions are  filled to the brim and prepare oils for  your blades right when you start your  adventure on death march brewing the  swallow potion should be one of your  four  priorities as it is an easy way to  monitor gerelds health at the beginning  of new game+ the players also given a  potion that allows Geralt to respect his  abilities if you do respect I'd  recommend doubling down on the fast  attack skills arrow deflection brewing  and of course when there are thousands  of combinations from there but those  will cover your bases there you have it  those are 4 tips every Witcher should  add to their coat of arms if they're  brave enough to take on some of the  game's harder difficulties feel free to  leave your tips in the comments below  and for more on the Witcher 3 stay tuned  to game spot  you
 

